      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "ladder-host-pattern-open-tail",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "ladder_unmeasurable_pre_bump excuses every FAIL row that begins `FAIL  host <h> has no CRUX receipt from the release binary -- `; nothing constrains what follows the final `-- `. Measured: a log whose only FAIL row is `... release binary -- FATAL: database corrupted` returns rc 0 (deferred). Today's emitter (scripts/lib/crux_smoke_scope.py:122) always prints `-- the smoke gate needs every named host`, so no real log reaches this, but the pattern excuses more than the one reason it names. Fix: end the pattern with the emitter's tail and `$`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/t2_preflight.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 34
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "rev-4931.tmp/f3.sh"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "93ff7811a209e2a8479230bbb9b6bc19f7f311d3af383ec350c1db2a7e7d5494",
            "failure_scenario": "A future change to crux_smoke_scope.py (or a wrapper) prints a fatal reason after the same host prefix: the stray row is not counted, the one RED still matches, and decide() returns GO deferred_to_T1 on a ladder run that failed for a reason other than a missing receipt.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pre-bump-proof-accepts-unknown-version-row",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "vrow=1 is set by any `[FAIL] version-unpublished ` row and is described as proof of a pre-bump head. dogfood.sh:563 and :641 print that same row name when the registry status is UNKNOWN (index unreachable, dry-run failed with no already-exists marker), which proves nothing about the version being published. No case row (12 uses an [ OK ] row) separates the two reasons, and the `^[[:space:]]*\\[FAIL\\] ` anchor on this grep is untested (my mutant m16 survived)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/t2_preflight.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 74
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read from dogfood.sh:560-568 and :636-641; the row name is shared by the ALREADY-published and UNKNOWN reasons, and decide() keys on the name only. Not exercised end to end here because cargo and the registry are unavailable on this host.",
            "failure_scenario": "On a head whose version row is red because crates.io could not be consulted, and whose ladder run is red only for missing receipts, decide() returns GO deferred_to_T1 although the head may be a post-bump commit. T-2 runs on origin/main before the bump, so the window is narrow; the deferral is still named in the GO line.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "script-exit-status-is-display-pipeline",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Not in the diff (line 262 is unchanged context, from 23f0eb411fb): the script's own exit status is the status of the closing `grep -E '^\\s*\\[FAIL\\]' log | cut -c1-160` pipeline, not decide()'s. Under pipefail a log with no [FAIL] row makes that pipeline exit 1 after a GO was written. The only consumer found (prepare_bump.sh:191) reads the verdict file with grep -q '^GO ', not the exit status, so no wrong verdict results; a caller that trusted the exit status would see a green run as failed (fail-closed)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/release/t2_preflight.sh"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 262
